# Project Overview

- ChainIQ: a supply chain analytics project using a publicly available dataset
- Goal: fill skill gaps from the last project, specifically data modelling, SQL transformation, and team delivery
- Scope: clean data, build a data model, SQL analysis, KPI development, Power BI dashboard and report
- Timeline: 4 to 6 weeks (deck shows 8 weeks as a conservative framework)

# Dataset and Tech Stack

- Dataset hosted publicly (uploaded in 2019), no API extraction or security concerns
- No external database (BigQuery/PostgreSQL skipped): everything hosted in GitHub
- Transformations in Python/PySpark; cleaning via Excel or preferred method
- SQL for analysis; Power BI for final dashboard and report
- Machine learning explicitly out of scope (planned for a future project)

# Analytical Focus Areas

- Six core questions:
  1. Fulfillment and SLA realism (realistic shipment times)
  2. Profitability from supplies
  3. Demand trends
  4. Product performance
  5. Prioritization based on findings
  6. Late deliveries and on-time performance
- KPIs to cover: revenues, discounts, margins, stock reorder points, month-to-month turnover

# Role Assignments

- Rebal: Power BI dashboard and report
- Samir: data cleaning (starts once added to GitHub)
- Samriti: SQL analysis and EDA
- Rotation logic: each person avoids repeating their last project role

# Deliverables and Workflow

- All data, analysis, and outputs pushed to GitHub (single source of truth)
- 6-page Power BI dashboard, executive recommendations, README with full findings
- Individual LinkedIn posts per step, rotating between team members
- Pitch deck to be shared in GitHub repo
